{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother","id":765301,"title":"Begotten and Wicked: Children of the Dark Mother","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-13T19:55:09-08:00","id":765301,"title":"Begotten and Wicked: Children of the Dark Mother","content":"I'm pretty sure I'm not the first person to ask this question. But for those who used the fan supplement Leviathan: The Tempest in their games, and those who are incorporating Beast: The Primordial as well, how exactly do you write off the (possible) relation between them? The Wicked Tribe were described in their write-up as the spawn of Tiamat, a name which happens to be one of several to refer to the Begotten's Dark Mother. Thoughts, anyone?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T10:01:36-08:00","id":765626,"title":"","content":"Both are mining similar mythological veins of inspiration, so some overlap is bound to occur. They are very likely related.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T10:44:26-08:00","id":765648,"title":"","content":"Leviathan's main point of distinction lies in that the monsters they are tend to be focused on cataclysm-these things destroy towns at the low end and end worlds on the high, and so reining them in is a big deal. Beasts are inclined to look at the closeness of them and might declare the first group to branch off, when mankind started becoming advanced enough to worry not just about their own death, but the death of the species. Nightmares of Extinction, if you will.<br /> <br /> They might consider them kin, but Leviathans put Beasts in a weird spot. Beasts are very much about accepting their monstrous state, embracing it and living it up. If Leviathans do that though, it invites calamity on a scale even Ravagars might not be comfortable with. Leviathans are the fragile or disabled kids in the family tree, and the Beast, bursting with energy and a need of play, just don't know quite what to do with them. They want to help, but it's apparent that they might make things worse from the word go.<br /> <br /> That's the best reading I can offer, anyways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T13:01:13-08:00","id":765731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=765648#post765648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Leviathan's main point of distinction lies in that the monsters they are tend to be focused on cataclysm-these things destroy towns at the low end and end worlds on the high, and so reining them in is a big deal. Beasts are inclined to look at the closeness of them and might declare the first group to branch off, when mankind started becoming advanced enough to worry not just about their own death, but the death of the species. Nightmares of Extinction, if you will.<br /> <br /> They might consider them kin, but Leviathans put Beasts in a weird spot. Beasts are very much about accepting their monstrous state, embracing it and living it up. If Leviathans do that though, it invites calamity on a scale even Ravagars might not be comfortable with. Leviathans are the fragile or disabled kids in the family tree, and the Beast, bursting with energy and a need of play, just don't know quite what to do with them. They want to help, but it's apparent that they might make things worse from the word go.<br /> <br /> That's the best reading I can offer, anyways.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is a pretty good point to start from. And yeah, Nightmares of Extinction is an apt title for the Wicked Tribe. With regards to Family Resemblance, the Makara in particular would be the Family most likely to develop close relationships with their 'fellow' Leviathans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T18:03:10-08:00","id":765929,"title":"","content":"Yep. I think Kings Raven actually mentioned how Beasts and Leviathans view each other:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668021#post668021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts of course think that Leviathans are Family; Leviathans are immune to Beast's first impression aura (Leviathan's are going to have really really strong psychic defences in 2E) but usually ok with having sane non-Leviathans who want to be around them. Beasts would make good middle management in a Cult. But in the tradition of WoD haughty and dismissive WoD steryotypes the Steryotype for Beasts will probably be something like:<br /> <br /> &quot;This girl walked into my temple and said her soul was a kraken too, and could she watch while I bathed. So I ate the creepy fucker's soul. It's funny, her soul actually was a kraken.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T21:22:44-08:00","id":766042,"title":"","content":"The thing about Leviathan being immune to the First Impression trait is straight up stupid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T06:50:49-08:00","id":766214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=766042#post766042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing about Leviathan being immune to the First Impression trait is straight up stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps bonuses for resisting it? Or maybe use the Wake mechanics as a basis?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T09:41:32-08:00","id":766320,"title":"","content":"No, I have a few gripes with that.<br /> <br /> 1) It's been acknowledged, several times now, that the thematic, iconic, and (in game and out of game) spiritual similarity of Beasts and Leviathan is obscenely close. Failing remembrance of Leviathan's mechanics be damned, they're so close that asserting it doesn't work doesn't make a lick of sense.<br /> <br /> 2)Speaking of, it's not a psychic phenomenon. Beast's powers are all spiritually based, so it's a spiritual effect.<br /> <br /> 3) This just smacks of the post-Imperial Mysteries mega-template debacle, or everyone making super vampires and changelings and stuff who's first order of power was to make it so Archmages couldn't do their shit. Which was stupid, because<br /> <br /> 4) A gameline saying another template can't do it's thing on another template kills narrative potential(I hear you on Demon, I'll get there in a second). Not only is it dis-empowering, it's <i>boring</i>. A Leviathan player misses out the joy of mystery and manipulation and emotionally based conflict by saying that Beast can't do what Beasts do. It treats a story hook like a curse, and that's the last thing you want to do.<br /> <br /> Now, what about Demon, you say?<br /> <br /> First off, that's Beast saying Beast can't do a thing rather than Demon saying Beast's can't do a thing. A gameline limiting itself is fine, narrative parameters create interest, and it works when everything else except humanity works. Secondly, Matt's super involved with Demon on top of deving Beast, so again, it feels legitimate. Third, Demon as a game of divine espionage has a lot of reasons to emphasize they are apart from the rest of the World of Darkness. Beast's rejection of them just strengthens Demon's narrative firmly places Demon as the Outsider, the stranger, the alien, the other, the <i>apart</i>. Leviathan doesn't have enough of that sort of framework to justify it.<br /> <br /> I mean, if you can justify it the way mages do, go for it, but even with my failed memory of Leviathan's mechanics, it's so clearly out of place it's...well, stupid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-15-2015, 02:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T20:23:13-08:00","id":766787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=766320#post766320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I have a few gripes with that.<br /> <br /> 1) It's been acknowledged, several times now, that the thematic, iconic, and (in game and out of game) spiritual similarity of Beasts and Leviathan is obscenely close. Failing remembrance of Leviathan's mechanics be damned, they're so close that asserting it doesn't work doesn't make a lick of sense.<br /> <br /> 2)Speaking of, it's not a psychic phenomenon. Beast's powers are all spiritually based, so it's a spiritual effect.<br /> <br /> 3) This just smacks of the post-Imperial Mysteries mega-template debacle, or everyone making super vampires and changelings and stuff who's first order of power was to make it so Archmages couldn't do their shit. Which was stupid, because<br /> <br /> 4) A gameline saying another template can't do it's thing on another template kills narrative potential(I hear you on Demon, I'll get there in a second). Not only is it dis-empowering, it's <i>boring</i>. A Leviathan player misses out the joy of mystery and manipulation and emotionally based conflict by saying that Beast can't do what Beasts do. It treats a story hook like a curse, and that's the last thing you want to do.<br /> <br /> Now, what about Demon, you say?<br /> <br /> First off, that's Beast saying Beast can't do a thing rather than Demon saying Beast's can't do a thing. A gameline limiting itself is fine, narrative parameters create interest, and it works when everything else except humanity works. Secondly, Matt's super involved with Demon on top of deving Beast, so again, it feels legitimate. Third, Demon as a game of divine espionage has a lot of reasons to emphasize they are apart from the rest of the World of Darkness. Beast's rejection of them just strengthens Demon's narrative firmly places Demon as the Outsider, the stranger, the alien, the other, the <i>apart</i>. Leviathan doesn't have enough of that sort of framework to justify it.<br /> <br /> I mean, if you can justify it the way mages do, go for it, but even with my failed memory of Leviathan's mechanics, it's so clearly out of place it's...well, stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I get what you're trying to say here. Better that a Beast's first impression aura and the Leviathan's Wake work as normal? That would certainly play to the themes of authority and control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T11:22:32-08:00","id":767168,"title":"","content":"Just a heads up, I don't look at the Beast forum that often so if you're going to ask Leviathan questions here it's best to shoot me a PM. I only noticed this because someone quoted me and that goes into my inbox.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=766042#post766042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing about Leviathan being immune to the First Impression trait is straight up stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a natural consequence of Leviathan having strong family themes that are completely incompatible with Beast: the Primordial's themes and a core principle that Leviathans don't get healthy relationships - giving a Leviathan a healthy relationship is taking away a Vampire's need for blood.<br /> <br /> In Beast the meaning of &quot;family&quot; comes from a modern western culture where family love and support each other. In Leviathan family is a bronze age political unit. As an example, in the Bible Laban sells his daughters in marriage in exchange for seven years of labour. That's the theme of &quot;family&quot; that Leviathan works off, and IMO it's completely incompatible with any interpretation of &quot;family&quot; that Changelings are happy to be a part of.<br /> <br /> Edit: A better example. In the origonal myths Tiamat gave birth to monsters who's only purpose was to try and kill her first set of children. I think Beasts would generally frown on using family as disposable cannon fodder. 1E Leviathan has a power for doing exactly that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=766320#post766320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) It's been acknowledged, several times now, that the thematic, iconic, and (in game and out of game) spiritual similarity of Beasts and Leviathan is obscenely close. Failing remembrance of Leviathan's mechanics be damned, they're so close that asserting it doesn't work doesn't make a lick of sense.</div> </div> </div> </div> Leviathan is about playing embodiments of mankind's savage, superstitious and destructive nature, struggling to exist in a world where civilisation has made you obsolete, and most probably destroying yourself and all of Somalia through your own flaws.<br /> <br /> I haven't actually figured out what Beast's core theme is supposed to be, but I'm pretty sure it's not supposed to be \u201c<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1a6lvMM6MLu3ObNwafZBEEXn51pu8k_8U1R2cjSeaNQk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Biblical Tragedy</a>\u201d<br /> <br /> Honestly from what I've seen of Beast it seems like the only thing it has in common with Leviathan is: The ability to have a cult. The fact Kraken is a valid character concept. Some similarities between Heroes and Ahabs. Honestly I'd say Leviathan is closer to Genius than Beast.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=766320#post766320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2)Speaking of, it's not a psychic phenomenon. Beast's powers are all spiritually based, so it's a spiritual effect.</div> </div> </div> </div> The Leviathan mental defence mechanic applies to everything that affects their mind or emotions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=766320#post766320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) This just smacks of the post-Imperial Mysteries mega-template debacle, or everyone making super vampires and changelings and stuff who's first order of power was to make it so Archmages couldn't do their shit. Which was stupid, because</div> </div> </div> </div> See my first section. This wasn't some reaction I came up with after Beast. It's a natural consiquence of pre-existing mecahnics and themes: Leviathan's incompatible interpreation of family and Leviathan's having mega psychic defences were both in 1E and thus predated Beast by years (In 1E it's Eye of the Eternal Storm / Citadel of the Doldrums, in 2E it's innate).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=766320#post766320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4) A gameline saying another template can't do it's thing on another template kills narrative potentia</div> </div> </div> </div> Sure, but I have to choose (and since the power is directly tied to the theme of family I do have to choose) between respecting another template or respecting the integrity of Leviathan's themes I'm going to go for Leviathan's themes every time; like all non-Beast WoD games I'm optimising for single splat play.<br /> <br /> If you want to play crossover you're priorities will be different and some adjustments will be needed. This is not the biggest issue, I do <i>not</i> envy whatever storyteller tries to balance a combat encounter for a mixed splat party including a Leviathan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 11-16-2015, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T11:27:27-08:00","id":767172,"title":"","content":"I feel comfortable in merely saying that I think you are wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T11:44:17-08:00","id":767178,"title":"","content":"About the game I wrote or about Beast: the Primordial?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T11:46:27-08:00","id":767180,"title":"","content":"If you're specifically taking other splats into account to shut down integral narrative options they have, you're not really optimizing for single splat play. You're optimizing for single splat verse supremacy, imo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 11-16-2015, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T11:56:56-08:00","id":767186,"title":"","content":"Why is that a bad thing?<br /> <br /> I always write for &quot;single splat verse supremacy&quot;, but it's always the splat I'm writing who get to be supreme. If I'm writing Leviathan then Leviathans are supreme but contrawise if I was ever writing Beast then I'd write from a Beast-supreme perspective where Leviathans fit the Beast cosmology as Nightmare of Societal Collapse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T12:03:05-08:00","id":767191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=767186#post767186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is that a bad thing?<br /> <br /> I always write for &quot;single splat verse supremacy&quot;, but it's always the splat I'm writing who get to be supreme. If I'm writing Leviathan then Leviathans are supreme but contrawise if I was ever writing Beast then I'd write from a Beast-supreme perspective where Leviathans fit the Beast cosmology as Nightmare of Societal Collapse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like you've taken an actually good attitude about game design and took it to it's unhealthiest degree.<br /> <br /> So to answer your earlier question, both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T12:06:47-08:00","id":767196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=767191#post767191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like you've taken an actually good attitude about game design and took it to it's unhealthiest degree.</div> </div> </div> </div>If saying that Leviathan's themes of family take priority over Beast's completely incompatible theme of family within the Leviathan setting is &quot;unhealthy&quot; then I think I'm quite comfortable being unhealthy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=767191#post767191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So to answer your earlier question, both.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, what do you think I got wrong about Leviathan?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 11-16-2015, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T12:29:27-08:00","id":767210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=767186#post767186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is that a bad thing?<br /> <br /> I always write for &quot;single splat verse supremacy&quot;, but it's always the splat I'm writing who get to be supreme. If I'm writing Leviathan then Leviathans are supreme but contrawise if I was ever writing Beast then I'd write from a Beast-supreme perspective where Leviathans fit the Beast cosmology as Nightmare of Societal Collapse.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a bad thing to me because from my perspective it's unhealthy for the world of darkness as a whole and the sharing of narrative space when applicable. Beast is not written with the other splats absolutely fitting the cosmology<i> beneath</i> them in terms of importance, and I don't think any game should be written with that perspective. It's not a contest. Leviathan can exist in Beast's cosmology and piece of the world, and Beast can exist in Leviathan's cosmology and piece of the world, without either being bent under the other. The propositions are not mutually exclusive. A game's protagonists <i>should</i> be the most important thing in its writing, but that is not the same as making them the most important thing in the toolbox setting.<br /> <br /> Archmage is the only official splat we have had that takes a heavier stance on that, but it makes concessions in the presentation of its place in the setting and the vulnerability of the other games in relation to it that allow the book to work, without necessarily infringing on the stage of other major supernatural beings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 11-16-2015, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T12:44:13-08:00","id":767225,"title":"","content":"And that is the crux of our disagreement. To me it is mutually exclusive, not usually, but in this specific instance it is mutually exclusive because Leviathan and Beasts have an insurmountable conflict in there themes of family.<br /> <br /> If I say that Beasts get their First Impressions then it contradicts Leviathan's theme of Family as a military-political alliance of people who don't actually like each other that much and the theme that Leviathans simply don't get to have healthy affirming relationships.<br /> <br /> And if I say that Beasts don't get their First Impressions it contradicts Beast's themes.<br /> <br /> <br /> Both you and Arc have made it clear that you disagree, but thus far neither of you have actually tried to convince me I'm wrong to say Beast and Leviathan's themes of family are mutually exclusive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T13:01:40-08:00","id":767240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=767225#post767225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I say that Beasts get their First Impressions then it contradicts Leviathan's theme of Family as a military-political alliance of people who don't actually like each other that much and the theme that Leviathans simply don't get to have healthy affirming relationships.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Healthy affirming relationships,&quot; he says.<br /> <br /> With the splat whose mechanics are basically set up to make their role in allied crossover play &quot;be the Bad Influence.&quot;<br /> <br /> With the splat whose examples of how they look to other supernaturals include &quot;one of them killed the mortal sister of their broodmate and the general response to this behavior was resignation&quot; and &quot;I nearly dipped into anthropophagy but one of them showed up seemingly to join in, so I figured that was a bad sign and ran for it.&quot;<br /> <br /> With the splat who directly stands to benefit from other supernaturals failing to keep a lid on their activities, has reason to actively encourage the reduction of the Traits most of those supernaturals use to measure their ability to function among human society, and whose &quot;happy ending&quot; for its sample character's running story is to become a mindless monster cut off from all regular contact with the outside world.<br /> <br /> &quot;Healthy affirming relationships.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T13:10:55-08:00","id":767254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=767225#post767225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I say that Beasts get their First Impressions then it contradicts Leviathan's theme of Family as a military-political alliance of people who don't actually like each other that much and the theme that Leviathans simply don't get to have healthy affirming relationships.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm... not sure why those can't coexist as opposite viewpoints? Beasts getting their First Impressions doesn't make the Leviathans' cultural perspective on Family any less valid, nor does it force them to have positive affirming relationships with Beasts (especially considering the Begotten are, as Satchel pointed out, often bad influences on other supernaturals in so far as dissociation from human consequences and motivations goes).<br /> <br /> And it would be an interesting avenue of conflict between them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 11-16-2015, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T13:12:28-08:00","id":767255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=767225#post767225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both you and Arc have made it clear that you disagree, but thus far neither of you have actually tried to convince me I'm wrong to say Beast and Leviathan's themes of family are mutually exclusive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I normally advocate the idea that you can't actually convince anyone of anything, but I'm in a mood where I actually believe it. I've said what I need to and don't much care beyond that point. You do you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T13:42:57-08:00","id":767297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=767225#post767225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that is the crux of our disagreement. To me it is mutually exclusive, not usually, but in this specific instance it is mutually exclusive because Leviathan and Beasts have an insurmountable conflict in there themes of family.<br /> <br /> If I say that Beasts get their First Impressions then it contradicts Leviathan's theme of Family as a military-political alliance of people who don't actually like each other that much and the theme that Leviathans simply don't get to have healthy affirming relationships.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beast <i>doesn't</i> have a theme of Family as healthy, affirming relationships. It has a theme of, &quot;You don't choose your family.&quot; They may well not like each other at all, and their relationships are often completely dysfunctional, but what do you expect out of a group of monstrous nightmare phobophages in human bodies? You can in fact have two different ideas of family represented in two different splats and not have either one invalidate the other, though. &quot;Different&quot; should not mean &quot;mutually exclusive.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if I say that Beasts don't get their First Impressions it contradicts Beast's themes. </div> </div> </div>If you really want Leviathans to be able to not be affected by Thicker Than Water, there's an easy way to resolve this. When power (x) says it does (y), and power (z) says it resists (y), doesn't that just become a Clash of Wills? The Beast rolls its Lair + (Highest Resistance Attribute). The Leviathan rolls its (Arete stat equivalent) + (Highest Resistance Attribute). Reroll ties. If the Beast wins the roll, Thicker Than Water applies as normal. If the Leviathan wins the roll, no good first impression from Thicker Than Water.<br /> <br /> Either way, it seems like you're making a huge deal out of a non-issue. Thicker Than Water is not mind control. It does not guarantee peace or good will. If a Beast acts like a jackass, it won't help her. It just means that, &quot;<i>all else being equal</i>, the Beast's impression level starts at good.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":8950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","user":"Vithrir","date":". 11-16-2015, 04:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T13:52:04-08:00","id":767304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=767254#post767254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm... not sure why those can't coexist as opposite viewpoints? Beasts getting their First Impressions doesn't make the Leviathans' cultural perspective on Family any less valid</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd say it does make Leviathan's viewpoint less valid, at least to an extent. I'm a <b>big</b> believer that mechanics should be there to help players get into the theme. An obvious example would be Promethian's Wasteland encouraging players to get into the theme of a nomadic game (The Wasteland might also be an example of taking this idea too far).<br /> <br /> The same goes for Thicker Than Water. If the mechanic is saying that because you're family you have a higher first impression, I'm taking that as guidance that I'm supposed to portray this theme of family in a certain way - and there's nothing wrong with that, unless you're playing a different splat with an exclusive theme.<br /> <br /> IMO if you want something to coexist as opposite in charachter viewpoints and draw conflict from the disagreement that's precisely when it's most important to not have mechanics that reinforce one side's viewpoint over the other. Having Leviathans and Beasts conflict over their different views of family is great, but if you want to do that I think you should make the setting an even ground to conflict on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=767254#post767254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> it force them to have positive affirming relationships with Beasts</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh it definately doesn't force anything. It just sends a message about the intended themes that's great for Beast and not so great for Leviathan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=767255#post767255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I normally advocate the idea that you can't actually convince anyone of anything, but I'm in a mood where I actually believe it. I've said what I need to and don't much care beyond that point. You do you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but you usually learn something from a good argument.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T13:53:40-08:00","id":767305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=767304#post767304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, but you usually learn something from a good argument.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Then maybe later, if other people don't make all the points I have. So far, they're saying it better than I would.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T14:14:06-08:00","id":767316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vithrir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=767297#post767297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you really want Leviathans to be able to not be affected by Thicker Than Water, there's an easy way to resolve this. When power (x) says it does (y), and power (z) says it resists (y), doesn't that just become a Clash of Wills?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm. I previously said Leviathan's get an automatic immunity because Thicker than Water dosen't have a dice pool.<br /> <br /> If Clash of Wills is used then because it affects their mind or emotions Leviathans would apply their defensive bonus - instead of rolling they get Sheol + Depth automatic successes.<br /> <br /> I think either way works fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vithrir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=767297#post767297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Either way, it seems like you're making a huge deal out of a non-issue. Thicker Than Water is not mind control. It does not guarantee peace or good will. If a Beast acts like a jackass, it won't help her. It just means that, &quot;<i>all else being equal</i>, the Beast's impression level starts at good.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest I thought it was a non-issue too since it only applies in crossover with Beast. But I thought since it's a non-issue I may as well honour Leviathans themes. But if nothing else this thread has convinced me it is important, and thus important to make the right decision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 11-16-2015, 05:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T14:50:19-08:00","id":767351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=767240#post767240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Healthy affirming relationships,&quot; he says.<br /> <br /> With the splat whose mechanics are basically set up to make their role in allied crossover play &quot;be the Bad Influence.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Cry me a river, this is dull. And overly simplistic. You do realize that recovering your fuel, or completing a quest, isn't exactly an evil act in of itself?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=767240#post767240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the splat whose examples of how they look to other supernaturals include &quot;one of them killed the mortal sister of their broodmate and the general response to this behavior was resignation&quot; and &quot;I nearly dipped into anthropophagy but one of them showed up seemingly to join in, so I figured that was a bad sign and ran for it.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because they're addicts, in a way. Their behavior is not, and does not, conform to mundane standards of morality, so it's useless to assume a willful malice when there's just no moral absolute that they are acting against.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=767240#post767240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the splat who directly stands to benefit from other supernaturals failing to keep a lid on their activities, has reason to actively encourage the reduction of the Traits most of those supernaturals use to measure their ability to function among human society, and whose &quot;happy ending&quot; for its sample character's running story is to become a mindless monster cut off from all regular contact with the outside world.<br /> <br /> &quot;Healthy affirming relationships.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This also assumes that neither party involved has a mutual interest in remaining unexposed. I don't see either character, in that situation, running to the authorities to report what they've seen, if they value their own hides. Also, there's nothing in Beast, apart from Chamber generation and direct Feeding, that requires another's Degeneration to work, so unless the Beast in question has an antagonistic relationship with another Supernatural, that really won't happen that often, at least, not at the Begotten's instigation. And, for all you know, Ben might have achieved the Incarnate Inheritance. And who said it was a &quot;happy&quot; ending, anyway.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Healthy, Affirming&quot; part of Beast is that they, through their Broods, and their relationships with other Supernatural Creatures, are able to come to terms with their own Hungers, and extend that acceptance to others. It may not necessarily be every Begotten's experience, and there is absolutely nothing stopping you from playing a toxic little shit, but while that's not the only way to play the Begotten, it is something to aspire to.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T14:57:48-08:00","id":767357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vithrir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=767297#post767297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Beast <i>doesn't</i> have a theme of Family as healthy, affirming relationships. It has a theme of, &quot;You don't choose your family.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm inclined to disagree. I'd say it's more like, &quot;Family is what you make of it,&quot; in that you can't trust blood relations (tyvfm, Satiety 1), but you can find others that you can, to a point. And the only ones who will, are other Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T15:21:41-08:00","id":767374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=767351#post767351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cry me a river, this is dull. And overly simplistic. You do realize that recovering your fuel, or completing a quest, isn't exactly an evil act in of itself?<br /> <br /> That's because they're addicts, in a way. Their behavior is not, and does not, conform to mundane standards of morality, so it's useless to assume a willful malice when there's just no moral absolute that they are acting against.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hex, you're interpolating a moral argument where none exists in a discussion about why it's incoherent to assert that having a default good impression with Leviathans in Social Maneuvering overly permits the Wicked Tribe to have a &quot;healthy and affirming&quot; relationship with a being whose nature is to play the enabler for hungers that the other gamelines (and mainstream Beast society, to a degree) overwhelmingly treat as things to be denied as much as possible or at least negotiated.<br /> <br /> Moral absolutes have absolutely nothing to do with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=767357#post767357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm inclined to disagree.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a direct quotation from the front of the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T16:05:10-08:00","id":767402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=767357#post767357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm inclined to disagree. I'd say it's more like, &quot;Family is what you make of it,&quot; in that you can't trust blood relations (tyvfm, Satiety 1), but you can find others that you can, to a point. And the only ones who will, are other Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm quoting the introduction to Beast (page 18), where it says the themes of Beast are: No Neat Little Boxes, You Don't Choose Your Family, and To Thine Own Self Be True.<br /> <br /> Family can indeed be what you make of it, and that idea and the pursuit of it is a perfectly good way to subvert the theme of &quot;You don't choose your family.&quot; This doesn't make &quot;you don't choose your family&quot; any less one of the explicitly stated themes of the game.<br /> <br /> (As an aside, I've always found that particular quote, 'To thine own self be true,' to be problematic. I mean, it sounds great, but Polonius isn't exactly someone I want to emulate... maybe he's more of a 'do as I say, not as I do' type character?)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T16:32:54-08:00","id":767417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=767374#post767374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hex, you're interpolating a moral argument where none exists in a discussion about why it's incoherent to assert that having a default good impression with Leviathans in Social Maneuvering overly permits the Wicked Tribe to have a &quot;healthy and affirming&quot; relationship with a being whose nature is to play the enabler for hungers that the other gamelines (and mainstream Beast society, to a degree) overwhelmingly treat as things to be denied as much as possible or at least negotiated.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how Begotten play the enabler. If they had some way to provoke Hungers in others, maybe, but you have one splat where hunting is a psychological necessity (Forsaken), another where it's the riskier fuel recovery option (requiem), and others still that need the kind of catharsis activities like those are necessary to stay level. I admit that I know next to nothing about Leviathan, but could you explain to me how accepting and guiding others through their impulses is less healthy and affirming than telling them to stop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T16:55:24-08:00","id":767434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=767417#post767417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">could you explain to me how accepting and guiding others through their impulses is less healthy and affirming than telling them to stop.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is certainly one way you can approach it. Maybe it's even an admirable way for a moral, enlightened character to approach it. But that isn't the default. All the actual rules say are that if you as a Beast accompany a supernatural being as it hunts, feeds, or both, you can gain Satiety by watching them. Could be a vampire stalking his prey in a ballroom, could be a werewolf pursuing an intruder in her territory, whatever, so long as the supernatural being in question is actively tracking prey and/or taking sustenance from a hunt. The supernatural being doesn't have to know you're there, but the hunt must be real a real act of predation (it can't be a vampire feeding on their own minion who is willing to be &quot;hunted&quot;, for example), and you must be physically present while observing it. The fact that it genuinely has to be an act of predation is going to make it much harder (but not impossible) for an enlightened and moral Beast to benefit from it, because in doing so they are subverting what the mechanics of the ability actually suggest, which is something altogether darker. And while a Beast may not have to be an enabler of the darker impulses of the various supernatural beings of the World of Darkness, being such an enabler is probably the easiest way to benefit from this ability.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ...<br /> I didn't include it in the above because I didn't want to represent your argument as a straw man version of itself, but now I have the image of Stuart Smalley as a Beast stuck in my head, offering daily affirmations to his tortured vampire friends as he comically accepts and guide them through their impulses, and it made me laugh, so thank you for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":8950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","user":"Vithrir","date":". 11-16-2015, 08:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T19:10:56-08:00","id":767519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vithrir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=767297#post767297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you really want Leviathans to be able to not be affected by Thicker Than Water, there's an easy way to resolve this. When power (x) says it does (y), and power (z) says it resists (y), doesn't that just become a Clash of Wills? The Beast rolls its Lair + (Highest Resistance Attribute). The Leviathan rolls its (Arete stat equivalent) + (Highest Resistance Attribute). Reroll ties. If the Beast wins the roll, Thicker Than Water applies as normal. If the Leviathan wins the roll, no good first impression from Thicker Than Water.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=767316#post767316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm. I previously said Leviathan's get an automatic immunity because Thicker than Water dosen't have a dice pool.<br /> <br /> If Clash of Wills is used then because it affects their mind or emotions Leviathans would apply their defensive bonus - instead of rolling they get Sheol + Depth automatic successes.<br /> <br /> I think either way works fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>This works, in my opinion. It reinforces the idea that the Begotten can't automatically strike a good rapport with the Leviathans, especially the well-established ones with high Sheol.<br /> <br /> And if a Beast encounters one of the Wicked Tribe while they're transformed into a lower Depth, their ability to strike a good first impression is stifled <i>on top of being scared senseless</i> by its true form if the Leviathan is at Depth 6.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T23:45:30-08:00","id":767611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=767374#post767374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">incoherent to assert that having a default good impression with Leviathans in Social Maneuvering overly permits the Wicked Tribe to have a &quot;healthy and affirming&quot; relationship</div> </div> </div> </div> Good thing I never said that then. This mechanic doesn't permit anything. It's simply a mechanic that reinforces themes of family - that family members like each other - that come from modern ideas of what a family is and thus conflicts with Leviathan's bronze age ideas of what a family is.<br /> <br /> Overall it has very little practical effect on the relationship between a Begotten and a Leviathan, it's purely about what message the mechanic sends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 11-17-2015, 02:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T07:28:00-08:00","id":767812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=767611#post767611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Good thing I never said that then. This mechanic doesn't permit anything. It's simply a mechanic that reinforces themes of family - that family members like each other - that come from modern ideas of what a family is and thus conflicts with Leviathan's bronze age ideas of what a family is.<br /> <br /> Overall it has very little practical effect on the relationship between a Begotten and a Leviathan, it's purely about what message the mechanic sends.</div> </div> </div> </div>And how the player behind the Beast roleplays. Because good first impression can quickly turn sour if one fumbles at a critical moment,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T07:45:10-08:00","id":767819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=767611#post767611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Good thing I never said that then. This mechanic doesn't permit anything. It's simply a mechanic that reinforces themes of family - that family members like each other - that come from modern ideas of what a family is and thus conflicts with Leviathan's bronze age ideas of what a family is.<br /> <br /> Overall it has very little practical effect on the relationship between a Begotten and a Leviathan, it's purely about what message the mechanic sends.</div> </div> </div> </div>I Know very little about Leviathians i'll admit... But how about making it so that the &quot;Thicker than Water&quot; Mechanics Work normally, but make the Leviathans feel uncomfortable about it, in essence it triggers normally but they by definition don't know/understand the way &quot;Family&quot; works with the Beasts and thus it makes then Distrustful (Instead of putting them on a level field and giving a good impression they leave a lingering discomfort or distaste about something they can't have.) Not sure if that would trigger or conflict with anything you've already put for them... but just an Idea.<br /> <br /> (The General thing would be it comes down to the ACTUAL impression the person leaves with a nagging feeling of annoyance about them being something similar and yet different. Or whatever.... I'm Making less sense as i write more.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T08:33:23-08:00","id":767839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=767611#post767611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Good thing I never said that then. This mechanic doesn't permit anything. It's simply a mechanic that reinforces themes of family - <b>that family members like each other</b> - that come from modern ideas of what a family is and thus conflicts with Leviathan's bronze age ideas of what a family is.<br /> <br /> Overall it has very little practical effect on the relationship between a Begotten and a Leviathan, it's purely about what message the mechanic sends.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure.<br /> <br /> Not in my game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T10:40:22-08:00","id":767937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vithrir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=767434#post767434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is certainly one way you can approach it. Maybe it's even an admirable way for a moral, enlightened character to approach it. But that isn't the default. All the actual rules say are that if you as a Beast accompany a supernatural being as it hunts, feeds, or both, you can gain Satiety by watching them. Could be a vampire stalking his prey in a ballroom, could be a werewolf pursuing an intruder in her territory, whatever, so long as the supernatural being in question is actively tracking prey and/or taking sustenance from a hunt. The supernatural being doesn't have to know you're there, but the hunt must be real a real act of predation (it can't be a vampire feeding on their own minion who is willing to be &quot;hunted&quot;, for example), and you must be physically present while observing it. The fact that it genuinely has to be an act of predation is going to make it much harder (but not impossible) for an enlightened and moral Beast to benefit from it, because in doing so they are subverting what the mechanics of the ability actually suggest, which is something altogether darker. And while a Beast may not have to be an enabler of the darker impulses of the various supernatural beings of the World of Darkness, being such an enabler is probably the easiest way to benefit from this ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinking more on this, I think you need to seperate &quot;healthy&quot; from &quot;moral&quot;. They're two entirely seperate things. For example you could argue that a Vampire who embraces being a Vampire (pun intended) and has a code about who they feed on is in a healthier state of mind than a vampire who hates being a vampire, hates herself, and only feeds on animals even though the second vampire has more ethical feeding habits.<br /> <br /> A Beast who encounters the second vampire and takes it upon themselves to convince her to start thinking like the first vampire strikes me as a very plausible concept.<br /> <br /> <br /> With Leviathan it's pretty straight forward. Ethically a Leviathan should avoid all human contact to avoid driving people insane through the Wake; however without human contact a Leviathan will faily quickly go mad and eventually become a Typhon. A Beast might encourage a Leviathan to come out of the wilderness and conquer a small town where something even worse than a Leviathan (Infernal Demons maybe) rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=767839#post767839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure.<br /> <br /> Not in my game.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can do what you like in your game. Personally when being &quot;close&quot; is a prerequisite for the Family Ties condition I take that as meaning you do need to like each other; that is the dictionary definition of close.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=767819#post767819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm Making less sense as i write more.)</div> </div> </div> </div>If I understand you, you're saying that they should get Thicker than Water but Leviathans get a Condition that makes things even worse between them later on? I think that would be even more of what the people arguing against Levaithan's resistance don't like.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T13:22:07-08:00","id":768052,"title":"","content":"I could see an argument for a Clay School merit to limit Wake effects (naturally with high prerequisites and a drawback). YMMV<br /> <br /> And I totes agree with that 2 vamps scenario.<br /> <br /> Reading threads like these make me think of Cornelius from Fight Club, e.g.: &quot;... Yes, these injuries are from fighting. Yes, I'm okay with that. I am enlightened.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T13:49:07-08:00","id":768069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=767937#post767937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can do what you like in your game. Personally when being &quot;close&quot; is a prerequisite for the Family Ties condition I take that as meaning you do need to like each other; that is the dictionary definition of close.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, that's not quite right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BtP Family Ties Sidebar</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is worth noting that the relationship does not have to be affectionate or even friendly for this Condition to apply; all it requires is that the Beast and the target be close. Associates, rivals, or even genial enemies thus potentially qualify for this condition as well, though it will likely be significantly harder to maintain more hostile connections.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T14:21:56-08:00","id":768099,"title":"","content":"Fair catch, but &quot;significantly harder to maintain more hostile connections&quot; is a clear statement that most Family Ties is between people who like each other - especially with the qualifier &quot;significantly&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=768052#post768052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see an argument for a Clay School merit to limit Wake effects (naturally with high prerequisites and a drawback).</div> </div> </div> </div>Anything of that nature would work better as an Evolution than a Merit IMO.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T15:24:40-08:00","id":768136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=767937#post767937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I understand you, you're saying that they should get Thicker than Water but Leviathans get a Condition that makes things even worse between them later on? I think that would be even more of what the people arguing against Levaithan's resistance don't like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of. What i meant and didn't put very well is that the sense of Family will put them on edge, likely make them paranoid about that first meeting, More likely leave a bad impression on the Leviathan. Nothing about their sense of Family says they should trust them and feeling that they can believe/trust this person without any evidence to show them how/why should make them slightly angry about it.<br /> <br /> They ARE Family and they Feel like it for the Beasts and Leviathans, just.. Leviathans don't like or Trust THEIR Family because they don't have the same type of Family as Beasts. It Won't effect the Beast's (That's what the Levi's Wake will do i assume, Not read it so i don't know) but it will effect the Leviathan, They don't have the same Societial norms... and as you Said to them family is a Political thing not something for comfort. They will not understand them fully.. not without having some justification first.<br /> <br /> I See that as not Stepping on Either of the two of their Niches. The Leviathans DO Feel a Sense of Family with Beast's.. but they are waiting for their family too call in Debts All the Time it might not happen and the Beast MIGHT Show themselves to be just what they need to keep them on the path they need to take.. But the Leviathan isn't going to like it at first. The Begotten/Beast on the Other hand feels all the things they would for other Family members.. and Isn't immune to being caught in the Leviathans Wake. They might end up just another Puppet for the Leviathans Cult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T18:02:10-08:00","id":768205,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=767819#post767819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I Know very little about Leviathians i'll admit... But how about making it so that the &quot;Thicker than Water&quot; Mechanics Work normally, but make the Leviathans feel uncomfortable about it, in essence it triggers normally but they by definition don't know/understand the way &quot;Family&quot; works with the Beasts and thus it makes then Distrustful (Instead of putting them on a level field and giving a good impression they leave a lingering discomfort or distaste about something they can't have.) Not sure if that would trigger or conflict with anything you've already put for them... but just an Idea.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=767937#post767937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I understand you, you're saying that they should get Thicker than Water but Leviathans get a Condition that makes things even worse between them later on? I think that would be even more of what the people arguing against Levaithan's resistance don't like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still preferring the idea of just Clash of Wills, with the Leviathan having the advantage of automatic successes in this roll. So, if a Beast is trying to strike a good impression by his nature alone, he's less likely to succeed with one of the Tribe than he would with another type of Kin.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=768136#post768136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I See that as not Stepping on Either of the two of their Niches. The Leviathans DO Feel a Sense of Family with Beast's.. but they are waiting for their family too call in Debts All the Time it might not happen and the Beast MIGHT Show themselves to be just what they need to keep them on the path they need to take.. But the Leviathan isn't going to like it at first. The Begotten/Beast on the Other hand feels all the things they would for other Family members.. and Isn't immune to being caught in the Leviathans Wake. They might end up just another Puppet for the Leviathans Cult.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps the Begotten could be less affected by the Wake than most other supernaturals? In 1E, a given supernatural's Advantage Trait has to be two dots or lower than a Leviathan's Sheol for him to be affected by the Wake. Not sure if that still applies in 2E, but perhaps a Beast with a Lair rating equal to, say, at least <i>half</i> the Leviathan's Sheol, rounded down, is immune to it? It would certainly reinforce the idea that the two splats are closely related, and even up the ante for a Leviathan who finds himself facing a Beast who doesn't bend to his presence.<br /> <br /> And it's even worse if he has the misfortune of facing down an <i>Apex</i> Beast. Because when things go sour and the Leviathan ends up changing shape to get the upper hand, he may have to go for a lower Depth if his adversary's Beast-Shape can match (or dwarf) him in size <i>and</i> possess a repertoire of abilities (Beast-Shape aspects, Atavisms, and Nightmares) which can go toe to toe with the Leviathan's Channels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T06:51:59-08:00","id":768472,"title":"","content":"My knee jerk reaction is thinking it's lame to say, &quot;My splat is immune to your splat.&quot; It sounds like little kids playing pretend, &quot;Nuh-uh! My ninja can dodge all of your guy's attacks! Yeah! Cuz I said so!&quot;<br /> <br /> Admittedly a gross simplification, that second bit.<br /> <br /> Still, as someone said upthread it's okay if <b>Beast</b> says that Beasts have trouble with Demons, but not if <b>Demon</b> says Beasts have trouble with Demons. Look at <b>Mummy</b> and <b>Hunter</b>: in the former it's explicitly stated any Mummy-flesh which is consumed has no magical infusion and is regurgitated; then the latter presents a supplement with Hunters that gain immortal powers by eating the god-flesh of Mummies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=767178#post767178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>About the game I wrote</b> or about Beast: the Primordial?</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that what these forums are half for? The audience arguing with the writers and developers on how the game should actually be? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T09:40:36-08:00","id":768566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=768472#post768472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look at <b>Mummy</b> and <b>Hunter</b>: in the former it's explicitly stated any Mummy-flesh which is consumed has no magical infusion and is regurgitated; then the latter presents a supplement with Hunters that gain immortal powers by eating the god-flesh of Mummies.</div> </div> </div> </div>A bit off-topic, but I always justified that bit by figuring that The Faithful of Shulpae are obviously using a magical rite to gain said powers, thus bypassing normal rules regarding ingestion of Mummy-meat. I mean, Shuanhksen gain powers from eating Mummies too, and Faithful gain power from eating pretty much <i>any</i> human-like supernatural, regardless of whether such is inherent to the being in question. More &quot;what the Faithful are doing&quot; and less &quot;eating Mummies gets you superpowers&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T11:09:57-08:00","id":768613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=768566#post768566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A bit off-topic, but I always justified that bit by figuring that The Faithful of Shulpae are obviously using a magical rite to gain said powers, thus bypassing normal rules regarding ingestion of Mummy-meat. I mean, Shuanhksen gain powers from eating Mummies too, and Faithful gain power from eating pretty much <i>any</i> human-like supernatural, regardless of whether such is inherent to the being in question. More &quot;what the Faithful are doing&quot; and less &quot;eating Mummies gets you superpowers&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, the Faithful's rules reference the amount of edible flesh on a target supernatural (which doesn't have to be &quot;dead&quot; at the time of consumption and in fact is mechanically incentivized to be as intact as possible), the sahu is a simulation of flesh made from memory and congealed necromancy, and Unclean Remains is pretty clearly an insurance quality against &quot;jackals ate your guildmaster's body when nobody was looking&quot; rather than a defensive measure against cannibalism for a splat whose principle antagonists specifically include cannibal mummies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T15:50:40-08:00","id":768759,"title":"","content":"The Wake does however make for a convenient source of Chambers. And a Leviathan Apex could make things interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T16:12:08-08:00","id":768770,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Like a possible story hook here...<br /> <br /> &quot;One of the Tribe hears word of a sea monster terrorizing the locale he's arrived in, and immediately assumes it's another Leviathan. So, he heads off to confront the entity, thinking it's a Typhon or an Ophion. But when he finally finds it, he realizes he's only <i>half</i>-right. The sea monster <i>is</i> a Leviathan, but <i>not </i>of the Tribe and bearing none of its weaknesses... And now, it plans to make him his next meal.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 11-18-2015, 07:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T23:48:23-08:00","id":769005,"title":"","content":"Do Apexes get to copy other splat's powers? I thought it was just a fancy word for the most powerful supernatural in the region and they shape the Primordial Dream somewhat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T00:12:42-08:00","id":769013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=769005#post769005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Apexes get to copy other splat's powers? I thought it was just a fancy word for the most powerful supernatural in the region and they shape the Primordial Dream somewhat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well there is also the Apex category of Beast. There isn't anything saying they can copy powers from other splats. That said Apex beasts are rare powerful and somewhat mysterious, so I wouldn't rule out that one may have powers similar to an ability from another splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T00:22:15-08:00","id":769019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=769013#post769013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well there is also the Apex category of Beast. There isn't anything saying they can copy powers from other splats. That said Apex beasts are rare powerful and somewhat mysterious, so I wouldn't rule out that one may have powers similar to an ability from another splat.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Especially if it's something they can mimic via the abilities of their Beast-Shape. Or Kinship Nightmares. That said, I am going to make a separate forum for homebrew ideas on an Apex Beast's Beast-Shape.<br /> <br /> <b>Update: Link</b><br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/769021-adopt-the-beast-shape-homebrew-abilities\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...brew-abilities</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 11-19-2015, 03:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T03:05:44-08:00","id":769068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=768566#post768566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A bit off-topic, but I always justified that bit by figuring that The Faithful of Shulpae are obviously using a magical rite to gain said powers, thus bypassing normal rules regarding ingestion of Mummy-meat.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bFair enough; I like that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=768613#post768613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Unclean Remains is pretty clearly an insurance quality against &quot;<b>jackals ate your guildmaster's body when nobody was looking</b>&quot; rather than a defensive measure against cannibalism for a splat whose principle antagonists specifically include cannibal mummies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I laughed aloud.<br /> <br /> More on-topic. I think any splat could justify immunity to that Beast's kinship power.<br /> <br /> For example, the whole <i>point</i> of Prometheans, after all, is that they're alone out there with only an enigmatic Principle that's maybe only sorta half watching out for them. Luckily no book in that line would ever say, &quot;These guys are immune to those guys because Disquiet et al&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T04:22:34-08:00","id":769097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=769068#post769068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, the whole <i>point</i> of Prometheans, after all, is that they're alone out there with only an enigmatic Principle that's maybe only sorta half watching out for them. Luckily no book in that line would ever say, &quot;These guys are immune to those guys because Disquiet et al&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Prometheans would <i>like</i> to have friends, and Disquiet happens to other people. And as spirits have already been established to be immune to Disquiet (thus proving it is possible), it opens the door for other beings to be immune as well. Such as Beasts, apparently.<br /> <br /> Of course, as stated, the kind of friend a Beast is likely to be is the one egging you on to go crazy/Torment and join up with the Stannum Refinement, if not Centimanus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 11-19-2015, 07:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T10:40:44-08:00","id":769393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=769068#post769068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, the whole <i>point</i> of Prometheans, after all, is that they're alone out there with only an enigmatic Principle that's maybe only sorta half watching out for them. Luckily no book in that line would ever say, &quot;These guys are immune to those guys because Disquiet et al&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I always felt that the point of Promethians was self discovery and exploration of humanity with lonelyness being secondary - The original Frankenstein's Monster did in fact have the one blind mentor who taught him a lot. 1E Promethian did say that Mages with the right Arcana could be practially immune to Disquiet.<br /> <br /> As for Leviathans. I was thinking that if you mix Primordial Water and Divine Fire very bad things happen. Disquiet would be redundant.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T11:26:44-08:00","id":769429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=769005#post769005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Apexes get to copy other splat's powers? I thought it was just a fancy word for the most powerful supernatural in the region and they shape the Primordial Dream somewhat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant in that way. The local dreamscape around powerful Wicked is likely to be wet, cold, dark, and maddening, even if the Leviathan in question isn't trying to give folks nightmares. While he may not be aware of the Begotten in his midst, emulating him, even developing Nightmares from his abilities, could tie the community together.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=769393#post769393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always felt that the point of Promethians was self discovery and exploration of humanity with lonelyness being secondary - The original Frankenstein's Monster did in fact have the one blind mentor who taught him a lot. 1E Promethian did say that Mages with the right Arcana could be practially immune to Disquiet.<br /> <br /> As for Leviathans. I was thinking that if you mix Primordial Water and Divine Fire very bad things happen. Disquiet would be redundant.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>More like the Disquiet never ends, IMHO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T14:10:01-08:00","id":769531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=769429#post769429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant in that way. The local dreamscape around powerful Wicked is likely to be wet, cold, dark, and maddening</div> </div> </div> </div> Don't forget tempestuous (pun intended), and yes indeed. The Wake is the Leviathan psychically pushing fear and obedience into the minds of everyone nearby. Psychic projection on that scale would have profound effects on the local dreamscape.<br /> <br /> One thing that's worth keeping in mind is that Leviathan rituals (and probably a few Channels in 2E) don't use Sympathy. They use Knowledge. The more you know about the Leviathan the easier it is to target you with Rituals. The origonal intent was to invoke the classic Lovecraft trope of &quot;don't ever read the occult tome!&quot; but if you can learn about the Leviathan from the dreamscape then Knowledge is Knowledge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=769429#post769429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More like the Disquiet never ends, IMHO.</div> </div> </div> </div>It ends when someone dies (which is quite likely)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}